  {
   "n": 8,
   "type": "MSQ",
   "section": "Technical",
   "tags": "Technical • Data Science and artificial Intelligence • +2 / -0",
   "html": "<p>Which of the following statements are true?</p>",
   "options": [
    {
     "key": "A",
     "html": "The sum of eigen values of square matrix is equal to the trace of a matrix."
    },
    {
     "key": "B",
     "html": "If a matrix is both symmetric and skew-symmetric is must be a null matrix."
    },
    {
     "key": "C",
     "html": "<p>\n\tThe transpose of square matrix <em>A</em> has the same eigen value as those of <em>A</em>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "key": "D",
     "html": "<p>\n\tThe inverse of an <em>n</em> × <em>n</em> matrix exists if and only if the rank is less than ‘<em>n</em>’.</p>"
    }
   ],
   "answer": [
    "A",
    "B",
    "C"
   ],
   "natRange": null,
   "answerText": "A, B, C",
   "marks": {
    "pos": 2,
    "neg": 0
   },
   "solution": "<p>(a, b, c)<br />\n(a) The sum of eigen values of square matrix is equal to the trace of a matrix.<br />\n(b) If a matrix is both symmetric and skew-symmetric is must be a null matrix.<br />\n(c) Eigen value of <em>A</em> and its transpose are the same.<br />\n(d) For a <em>n</em> &times; <em>n</em> matrix, inverse exists only if rank = <em>n</em>.</p>"
  },
